      ":question/id": "17f24d34-b565-5380-9f26-8e638b938a76",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Write the following first-order linear ODE in standard form.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} \\cos{(6 x )} + 6 y \\sin{(6 x )} + 4 \\sin{(12 x )}=0\\,.\n$$\n\nAssume $\\cos{(6 x )}\\ne 0$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "A first-order linear ODE is in standard form if it is written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x).\n$$\n\nConverting the given equation to standard form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} \\cos{(6 x )} + 6 y \\sin{(6 x )} + 4 \\sin{(12 x )}=0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} \\cos{(6 x )} + 6 y \\sin{(6 x )}=- 4 \\sin{(12 x )} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} + \\frac{6 y \\sin{(6 x )}}{\\cos{(6 x )}}=- \\frac{4 \\sin{(12 x )}}{\\cos{(6 x )}} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} + 6 y \\tan{(6 x )}=\\frac{- 8 \\sin{(6 x )}\\cos{(6 x )}}{\\cos{(6 x )}} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\underbrace{(6 \\tan{(6 x )})}_{P(x)}y=\\underbrace{- 8 \\sin{(6 x )}}_{Q(x)}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nNow, the equation is written in standard form with $P(x)=6 \\tan{(6 x )}$ and $Q(x)=- 8 \\sin{(6 x )}.$",
